WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.130
(upbeat music)

2
00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.750
- [Announcer] Whenever
you talk to your device

3
00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.660
and it understands what you say,

4
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.970
whether it's to set a
reminder, open an app,

5
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.610
or use dictation, that's
speech recognition.

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.730
We want to keep making speech recognition

7
00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:17.350
better for everyone in every language.

8
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.900
We use recorded voice clips

9
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.860
contributed by people around the world

10
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.053
to train our speech recognition models.

11
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.210
When you contribute voice clips with us,

12
00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:29.073
we also do something
called de-identification.

13
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.520
If we identify a long string of numbers

14
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.230
like a social security
number, a credit card number,

15
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:37.040
or something like an email address,

16
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.963
our cloud-based technology
automatically deletes it.

17
00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.010
We also remove any association

18
00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.580
between your voice
clips and your user IDs,

19
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.030
like your Microsoft accounts.

20
00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:50.770
Your de-identified voice
clips are saved along

21
00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:53.070
with many others from
people around the world.

22
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.970
With your permission,

23
00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.350
people might review or
listen to your voice clips

24
00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.530
and make transcriptions of them.

25
00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:02.350
We randomly select voice clips

26
00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.800
to train our machine learning models.

27
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.260
This helps make our speech
recognition technology

28
00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.270
better at recognizing and interpreting

29
00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.580
the nuances of how real people talk

30
00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.660
like accents and regional pronunciation.

31
00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:18.090
Anything we don't use, we
delete after two years.

32
00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.640
But when a voice clip is
used to train our models

33
00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.570
we keep it for longer than two years,

34
00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.810
so we can keep making
longterm improvements

35
00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.530
to our speech recognition products.

36
00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:29.060
Only Microsoft employees

37
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.850
and people working at other companies

38
00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:33.400
contracted to operate
on Microsoft's behalf,

39
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.130
can listen to voice clips.

40
00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.540
We work to make sure all
the voice clips we use

41
00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:41.343
are protected and secure
through this whole process.

42
00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.460
To help further protect your privacy,

43
00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:45.600
if we encounter something

44
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.470
that sounds like personal
information in a voice clip,

45
00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:49.863
Microsoft will delete it.

46
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.860
It's up to you if you want
to allow this kind of review,

47
00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.550
you can still use our products
no matter what you choose.

48
00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.260
Microsoft is committed to
building exceptional products

49
00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:04.200
for the way people really
work, talk, and use technology.

50
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.700
If you do choose to contribute
your voice clips for review,

51
00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:08.640
thank you!

52
00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.550
You'll be helping make speech
recognition work even better

53
00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.683
for you and everyone else.
